      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm trying to fix up my linkedin \"about\" section so i can get past the automated filters at the big tech firms. they use these ATS systems that rank us based on \"term coverage\"—basically how many specific keywords we have. \n\nthe score it gives is just based on the fraction of these terms that show up in my bio. i really need a high score to get noticed, but PLEASE don't just make it a list of words or keyword-stuff it. if it looks like a bot wrote it, the recruiters will just ignore me. it needs to actually read like a real, professional bio.\n\ncan you rewrite this for me? here are the terms i need to hit: \n\nAgile, Scrum, Python, AWS, Cloud Architecture, Stakeholder Management, Machine Learning, Data Pipelines, Cross-functional Leadership, CI/CD, SQL, and Strategic Planning.\n\nhere is my current draft:\n\"I am a software engineer with 5 years of experience. I like building scalable systems and working with teams to solve complex problems. I have experience with backend development and helping manage projects.\"",
